  "provenance": {
    "physical_parameters": {
      "origin": "inferred",
      "note": "Lister Petter TR1-style direct-injection, naturally aspirated single-cylinder working variant. Manufacturer TR Industrial Engines TDS (10739), pp. 4-6: bore 98.42 mm, stroke 101.6 mm, 0.773 litre, compression ratio 15.5:1, minimum idle 850 RPM, air cooling and variable speeds through 2500 RPM. https://listerpetter.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/10739-TR-Industrial-Engines-TDS.pdf . Full fuel 29 mg/cycle approximates 1.6-2.5 litre/hour at 1500-2500 RPM using the sheet density 0.84 kg/litre; this is an inference, not a measured injection trace. Fuel LHV 42.7 MJ/kg follows that sheet. Injection start 22 degrees BTDC is a working approximation informed by the TR1 research configuration in Fayad (2017), University of Birmingham, p. 74, https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/id/eprint/7919/1/Fayad17PhD.pdf . Pulse duration, rod length, valve effective areas/windows, reservoir and thermal state, and combustion coefficients are authored. Intake 340-580 degrees and exhaust 130-378 degrees preserve breathing around gas-exchange TDC. Not a validated TR1 pressure, torque or governor model."
    },
    "presentation": {
      "origin": "artistic",
      "note": "Separate single-cylinder acoustic variant using the shared version 11 diesel runtime. Author Benboncan describes Lister Startup And Idle.wav as a stationary Lister firing then idling as its centrifugal governor engages: https://freesound.org/people/Benboncan/sounds/89724/ . The recording does not identify a TR1, exact engine model, cylinder count or RPM; it is a character reference, not proof of this hardware or a calibrated acoustic target. The recording is CC BY 4.0 and contains no embedded material in this definition or generated carrier. Authored smaller-block modes, single short lossy exhaust branch, pressure-driven texture, smooth valve contacts and pumping breath give the single-cylinder timing its own radiation response. Loaded rounding and zero-fuel flow/mechanical layers reuse the accepted Ural mechanisms with separate parameter values. No recorded PCM, measured impulse response, physical cooling fan, within-cycle speed ripple or solved governor is embedded. Mean RPM and fueling remain externally controlled."
    }
  }
